  <!-- ===== FAQ ===== -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl text-charcoal-900 font-bold mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <p class="text-steel-500">What buyers ask before ordering.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-steel-100 p-5 group shadow-sm">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-charcoal-900 text-base">How do I choose the right model?</h3>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-steel-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Pick by seed type or scenario above. Every standard model presses most oil seeds — the difference is pressing force (harder seeds need larger tonnage) and barrel config (single for startup, double for commercial). For sesame use the Sesame Special, for coconut milk use the 300 Type Coconut.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-steel-100 p-5 group shadow-sm">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-charcoal-900 text-base">Does a higher model number mean more kg per batch?</h3>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-steel-600 text-sm leading-relaxed"><b>No.</b> Every standard model holds the same 100 kg per batch (390 mm barrel). Higher model number = more pressing force for harder seeds. To press more batches per shift, add a double barrel — not a bigger model number.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-steel-100 p-5 group shadow-sm">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-charcoal-900 text-base">Single or double barrel?</h3>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-steel-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Startup / testing market → single barrel (lower cost, compact). Commercial / continuous operation → double barrel (one presses, other loads, eliminates idle time between batches). Double barrel doesn't press 2 batches at once — it shares one hydraulic system between two barrels.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-steel-100 p-5 group shadow-sm">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-charcoal-900 text-base">What's the difference between cold press and hot press?</h3>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-steel-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Cold press (HN426+) extracts oil <b>without heating seeds</b> — preserves nutrients, flavor, color for premium-grade oil. Hot press roasts seeds first for faster yield at standard prices. Cold press can also do hot press; hot press cannot do cold press.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-steel-100 p-5 group shadow-sm">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-charcoal-900 text-base">Can I upgrade from single to double barrel later?</h3>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-steel-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-steel-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Yes. The hydraulic system is the same — you can start with a single barrel HN325 and add a second barrel later when your order volume grows. This is why many startups begin with HN300 or HN325 single barrel and upgrade to double barrel within 6-12 months.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

